# Views and Templates Rule

- Use Greek labels and section headings for user-facing screens.
- Keep section numbering visible in relevant screens (for example `10.1`, `10.4.6`).
- Record pages should expose history access (direct tab/section or link to filtered history).
- Enforce role/permission checks in views and actions.
- Keep forms explicit and traceable to requirement fields; avoid hidden business logic in templates.
